post_install() {
    cat <<'EOF'

  aetherprompt is installed. To activate it:

  GPG (passphrase prompts for signing/decryption):
      add to ~/.gnupg/gpg-agent.conf:
        pinentry-program /usr/bin/aetherprompt
      then run:
        gpgconf --kill gpg-agent
      test:  echo test | gpg --clearsign

  SSH (private-key passphrase prompts, git push/pull over ssh):
      export SSH_ASKPASS=/usr/bin/aetherprompt
      export SSH_ASKPASS_REQUIRE=force     # 'prefer' to only use without tty
      (put these in ~/.profile or your Hyprland env config; the ssh-askpass
       subcommand is selected automatically by how the program is called)

  SUDO:
      export SUDO_ASKPASS=/usr/bin/aetherprompt
      then run: sudo -A <command>

  Optional — Hyprland blur, add to hyprland.conf:
      layerrule blur, match:namespace aetherprompt-prompt
      layerrule ignore_alpha 0.3, match:namespace aetherprompt-prompt

  Colours follow your active caelestia scheme automatically.

EOF
}
